---
import MissionLayout from '../../layouts/MissionLayout.astro';
---

<MissionLayout
  slug="bom-bom-singapore"
  heading="BOM BOM SINGAPORE"
  timeline="Jun – Sep 2026"
  status="Live"
  statusHref="https://bombom.com"
  heroImage="/assets/projects/bom-bom-hero.webp"
  explorerGradient="linear-gradient(40deg, #210913 0%, #57152c 100%)"
>
  <section class="case-section">
    <h2 class="case-section-title">1. The TL;DR <span class="case-section-sub">(Executive Summary)</span></h2>
    <div class="case-field">
      <h3 class="case-field-label">The Purpose</h3>
      <p class="case-field-value">Revamp the digital experience for BOM BOM, a Singapore-based fresh pet-food brand offering personalised meals for dogs and cats. Make the brand's nutrition expertise, whole ingredients, and convenient delivery easier for pet parents to understand and explore.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="case-field">
      <h3 class="case-field-label">Role &amp; Responsibilities</h3>
      <p class="case-field-value">Lead Designer for the brand and its website revamp, leading UX research, UI execution, and development coordination. The project ran from June to September 2026, with the revamped experience launching in September 2026.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="case-field">
      <h3 class="case-field-label">The Design Challenge</h3>
      <p class="case-field-value">Choosing a fresh-food plan involves more than choosing a flavour. Pet parents need to understand ingredients, personalisation, portions, pricing, storage, and delivery before committing. The design challenge is to make that information approachable while keeping the route to a meal plan clear.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="case-field">
      <h3 class="case-field-label">The Solution</h3>
      <p class="case-field-value">A brand-led website that connects pet and food photography with clear nutrition education, customer stories, transparent pricing, and prominent calls to start a customised meal plan.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="case-field">
      <h3 class="case-field-label">The Impact</h3>
      <p class="case-field-value"><strong>30% more website visitors and 20% more returning visitors one month after launch.</strong> Early post-launch results for the revamped website.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="case-section">
    <h2 class="case-section-title">2. Strategy &amp; Discovery</h2>
    <div class="case-field">
      <h3 class="case-field-label">UX Research</h3>
      <p class="case-field-value">Led UX research for the revamp, alongside responsibility for UI execution and development coordination. The experience connects the questions pet parents face when exploring fresh food with product education, pricing, and a clear meal-plan entry point.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="case-field">
      <h3 class="case-field-label">Brand Context</h3>
      <p class="case-field-value">BOM BOM has offered customised fresh pet food in Singapore since 2017. Its proposition combines meals tailored to each pet's profile with nutritionist formulation, pre-portioned packs, delivery, and ongoing support.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="case-field">
      <h3 class="case-field-label">Audience &amp; Information Needs</h3>
      <p class="case-field-value">The experience serves dog and cat owners exploring fresh feeding, including those considering their pet's age, size, preferences, and sensitivities. Dedicated food, pricing, and feeding-guide pages let visitors investigate practical questions before ordering.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="case-field">
      <h3 class="case-field-label">Experience Strategy</h3>
      <p class="case-field-value">The revamped site moves from a simple brand promise into ingredient transparency, personalisation, and supporting evidence. Product education and customer stories sit alongside pricing and ordering entry points, balancing reassurance with action.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="case-section">
    <h2 class="case-section-title">3. Execution <span class="case-section-sub">(The &ldquo;How&rdquo;)</span></h2>
    <div class="case-field">
      <h3 class="case-field-label">Design Leadership</h3>
      <p class="case-field-value">Led UI execution and coordinated development for the website revamp, carrying design responsibility through to the September 2026 launch.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="case-field">
      <h3 class="case-field-label">Visual Direction</h3>
      <p class="case-field-value">The live design pairs bold berry-red headlines and calls to action with warm neutrals, rounded forms, and expressive pet photography. Close-up food imagery makes the ingredients tangible, while the approachable visual language keeps a technical nutrition topic welcoming.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="case-field">
      <h3 class="case-field-label">Information Architecture</h3>
      <p class="case-field-value">Navigation separates Why Fresh, Our Food, Real Results, Pricing, and About Us. This gives visitors distinct routes to learn about the category, examine the product, explore customer experiences, and understand the brand.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="case-field">
      <h3 class="case-field-label">Meal-Plan Journey</h3>
      <p class="case-field-value">Prominent ordering calls to action connect the marketing site to BOM BOM's meal planner. The pricing page presents pet-size tiers, meal portions, plan inclusions, and a cost estimator, while account access gives existing customers a separate entry point.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="case-section">
    <h2 class="case-section-title">4. Experience Highlights</h2>
    <div class="case-field">
      <h3 class="case-field-label">Confidence Before Commitment</h3>
      <p class="case-field-value">Ingredient explanations, nutrition-team profiles, and customer stories provide different ways to explore the brand's approach. These are presented as brand and customer content, rather than as evidence of the redesign's commercial impact.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="case-field">
      <h3 class="case-field-label">Practical Support</h3>
      <p class="case-field-value">Feeding and storage guidance, FAQs, and BB Support address the practical side of switching food. The experience extends beyond selecting a product to helping pet parents understand how it fits into everyday life.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="case-field">
      <h3 class="case-field-label">Explore the Live Experience</h3>
      <ul class="case-field-list">
        <li><a class="case-link" href="https://bombom.com/sg/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Homepage</a> &mdash; brand introduction and meal-plan entry point.</li>
        <li><a class="case-link" href="https://bombom.com/sg/our-food/overview" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Our Food</a> &mdash; ingredient transparency and personalisation.</li>
        <li><a class="case-link" href="https://bombom.com/sg/our-pricing" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Pricing</a> &mdash; plan comparison and cost estimation.</li>
        <li><a class="case-link" href="https://bombom.com/sg/about-us" target="_blank" rel="noopener">About Us</a> &mdash; the brand's origin and nutrition team.</li>
      </ul>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="case-section">
    <h2 class="case-section-title">5. Visual Highlights</h2>
    <div class="case-field">
      <h3 class="case-field-label">The Revamped Website</h3>
      <p class="case-field-value">Screenshots of the live homepage, food overview, and pricing page, captured in October 2026.</p>
      <div class="gallery-wrap" role="region" aria-label="BOM BOM website screenshots">
        <div class="gallery-track-wrap">
          <div class="gallery-track">
            <img class="gallery-img" src="/assets/projects/bom-bom-homepage.webp" alt="BOM BOM homepage with a berry-red headline, pet and food photography, and a custom-meal ordering button" loading="lazy" />
            <img class="gallery-img" src="/assets/projects/bom-bom-our-food.webp" alt="BOM BOM food overview introducing fresh meals for dogs and cats" loading="lazy" />
            <img class="gallery-img" src="/assets/projects/bom-bom-pricing.webp" alt="BOM BOM pricing page comparing customised meal plans by pet size" loading="lazy" />
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="gallery-controls">
          <button class="gallery-btn" type="button" aria-label="Previous screenshot">&#8592; Back</button>
          <span class="gallery-counter" aria-live="polite" aria-atomic="true">1 / 3</span>
          <button class="gallery-btn" type="button" aria-label="Next screenshot">Next &#8594;</button>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="case-section">
    <h2 class="case-section-title">6. Outcome &amp; Lessons</h2>
    <div class="case-field">
      <h3 class="case-field-label">Early Outcome</h3>
      <ul class="case-field-list">
        <li><strong>30% increase in website visitors</strong> one month after launch.</li>
        <li><strong>20% increase in returning visitors</strong> over the same post-launch window.</li>
      </ul>
    </div>
    <div class="case-field">
      <h3 class="case-field-label">Design Takeaway</h3>
      <p class="case-field-value">For a personalised product, the experience needs to explain the offer as clearly as it presents the brand. This revamp brings visual warmth, product detail, practical guidance, and a direct ordering path into one connected experience.</p>
    </div>
  </section>
</MissionLayout>
